// Core task-lifecycle vocabulary (task runtime TR2).
//
// `Task<T>` is the owned lifecycle CLAIM for one provider-held activation. It
// is deliberately not a stack, continuation frame, pool slot, or scheduler
// object. The runtime/provider layers establish values of this type; this core
// module only gives the claim a source home.
//
// The integer fields are the bootstrap carrier for provider and activation
// identity. They are not public proof that a provider accepted custody: TR4's
// boundary requirement and admission path own establishment of real claims.
data Task<T> [linear] {
    provider: u64;
    activation: u64;
}

// TaskOutcome<T> and StartOutcome<T, Arguments> deliberately do not ship in
// this rung. Their generic payloads must propagate the substituted argument's
// multiplicity: Returned(LinearT) and Rejected(LinearArguments) cannot erase
// a debt merely because the generic declaration cannot see the substitution.
// Land those sums with qualifier-aware generic payload propagation, then add
// the TaskRuntime boundary operations in TR4.
